==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*cüvä}} (compare {{cog|et|süva}}), probably from {{inh|fi|fiu-pro|*tiwä}} (compare e.g. {{cog|se|davvi||north}}, {{cog|mhr|тӱнӧ}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Adjective===
{{fi-adj|syv|empi|in}}

# [[deep]]
#: {{ant|fi|matala|q1=see usage notes}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''syvä''' joki|a '''deep''' river}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''syvä''' kulho|a '''deep''' bowl}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''syvä''' haava|a '''deep''' wound}}
#: {{uxi|fi|'''syvällä''' joessa|'''deep''' in the river}}
#: {{uxi|fi|'''syvälle''' maan uumeniin|'''deep''' into the bowels of the earth}}
#: {{uxi|fi|siemenet ovat '''syvässä'''|the seeds are in '''deep'''}}
#: {{uxi|fi|kumartaa '''syvään'''|to bow '''deep(ly)'''}}
# [[deep-water]]
#: {{ant|fi|matala}}
#: {{uxi|fi|[[syväsatama|'''syvä'''satama]]|'''deep-water''' harbour}}
# [[deep]], [[profound]]
#: {{ant|fi|pinnallinen}}
#: {{ux|fi|Oppilaidemme ylpeys koulustaan on hyvin '''syvällä'''.|Our students' sense of pride in the school goes very '''deep'''.}}

